e98e26c", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be topological spaces.\nConsider the rule <MATH_0003> which associates to\nthe open <MATH_0004> the set\n<MATHSEG_0001> is continuous<MATHSEG_0002>\nwith the obvious restriction mappings. We claim that\n<MATH_0005> is a sheaf. To see this suppose that\n<MATH_0006> is an open covering, and\n<MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008> with\n<MATH_0009> for all <MATH_0010>.\nIn this case define <MATH_0011> by setting <MATH_0012>\nequal to the value of <MATH_0013> for any <MATH_0014> such that\n<MATH_0015>. This is well defined by assumption. Moreover,\n<MATH_0016> is a map such that its restriction to <MATH_0017>\nagrees with the continuous map <MATH_0018>. Hence clearly <MATH_0019> is\ncontinuous!\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:017a127edad67e6dc74de1c67d24816489c220f94b02da225d71397164db9d2e", "unit_id": "inventory:sheaves:006V:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:bc3027f83e6b052397a9045a9809a9a22d10425c3e9660861ee033573a88da96", "hash": "sha256:bc3027f83e6b052397a9045a9809a9a22d10425c3e9660861ee033573a88da96", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 26882, "byte_start": 26359, "file": "sheaves.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:383b7829984aa6a548532d38bbe8fe281cb3686ce83c1633e15b6b9d50955888", "line_end": 790, "line_start": 776}, "owner_tag": "0073", "parent_tag": "0071", "requested_label": "sheaves-lemma-sheaves-structure", "requested_tag": "0073", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0071", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-sheaves-structure}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\